es:\n\nType - SITUATION (情境):\n1. 「巷子深处，一锅红烧肉刚出锅」 (workable pure visual; a bit calm.)\n\nType - INFORMATION:\n2. 「红烧肉想不腻，先把这勺汁收明白」 —hmm info claim not aligned actual video. This promises viewer learns why no grease. Such process info must in video to \"get\" info; not known. Probably not authorized. Instead maybe not.\n\nWhat info might be delivered: The claim 12年/“老手艺不是随便做” - not info in 40 sec? Sensory not info. According to PP-1, if no info available, only use visual types: Situation + Quote (not usable) =&gt; technically only one candidate? But that left us alone. However there are two real source info bits the content can deliver when the video includes caption that clearly said (owner-proposed): \"卖了12年\" (fact anchor, self-attested); \"自己腌黄酒糟卤打底\" informational: This gives INFORMATION candidates:\n- 「这锅肉香在哪？自家腌的糟卤，第 12 年」 hmm '香在哪' answer in caption...\n- 「加的黄酒是自家腌的——这锅肉我们做了 12 年」\nBut direct \"12年/糟卤\" titles emphasize information that could arouse curiosity? Wait by contrast title should be teaser: not 摘要: e.g., 「为什么这锅红烧肉值得你记一家店」 no.\nInformation type (承诺你将拿到一条信息): If video caption reveals how it achieves shine/no greasiness: Wait actual video only出锅; no recipe steps visible. It can't \"make you可学到\". So INFORMATION hook ungrounded... but title may promise the info \"what's the last pour\"? If reveals? If the clip visible shows but doesn't explain, paradoxically curiosity: Why pouring? They are \"the last spoon of juice\" could trigger wanting to understand; hmm.\n\nUse CONTRADICTION type:\n「越肥的五花，越怕不用心的人做」hmm philosophical: contradiction: 怕肥的碰到真香的打脸? \"怕吃肥肉的人，在这家店门口站了三秒\" — invents behavior.\nBetter CONTRADICTION:\n「烧了十二年的红烧肉，最怕的不是费火，是省事」— a \"contradiction\"? Sort of claim: 12-year cook's fear. not exactly contradiction; phrase \"红烧肉从来不是烧出来的是等出来的\"? hmm.\n\nHonestly: present candidate list relying mainly on situation and simple factual-tease. PP allows all entries but recommended title must be supported by正文. Our正文 we don't have (met) - so list draft-title candidates apply A/B route.\n\nA-Route titles (no background claims):\n- A1 SITUATION: 「滴着油的这锅肉，刚出锅」 hmm title with \"滴油\" delightful? hmm Food writing: \"红烧肉出锅那四十秒\" good.\n- A2 QUOTABLE_LINE: if not there's quote; maybe we use sensory as quote? no.\nA-Route recommends: 「看清了，肉是这样出锅的」 hmm weird.\nFood leading - \"这锅肉，端上桌前先抖给你看\"(the wobble shot - quivering). But \"抖动\" already visual itself \"你看这块肉的颤劲\" → Captions? \"你看它这个颤劲儿\" sounds like a Bilibili food narrator; A frame.\nBetter title type IDENTITY:\n- D「8张桌的小店，一锅肉做了12年」 identity + craft. Actually a strong factual title but with \"12年\". It fits user wants \"老手艺可信\" better. That's B route/D not \"identity\"? hmm.\n\nDraft set:\nA-轨 (食欲/画面)\n1. SITUATION 「红烧肉出锅的最后40秒」 — summary-ish? no: final still gives position, conveys \"you will see the final instant\"; open gap: 40s - what happens? Actually summary: not \"看完你就知道了\"; title describing itself (a 40-sec clip of removing pot?) In recommendation explanation: 正文的第一秒就能兑现：画面上就是那锅肉正在出锅，标题承诺的与正片一致 — OK not摘要? \"最后40秒\" doesn't reveal result, implies climax. Works.\n2. SITUATION alt 「这锅肉，抖一下你就知道有多糯」 hmm adds \"糯\" claim from watching. It promises visible wobble; in PRE need frame confirm. Perhaps weird.\n3. CONTRADICTION 「越是红烧肉，越不能急」 for craft; but not visible enough.\n\nhmm, maybe we produce 2 route... Let's instead craft solid clean C-family.\n\nOption B family (资历/手艺) title recommended:\n「本地人吃了12年的红烧肉，就在这条巷子里」\nWait \"本地人\" ungrounded. avoid:\n「一道红烧肉，在这条巷子里卖了12年」good:\nLocation: \"老城区这条巷子\" vague but exactly store. \"卖\" phrasing. This claims only \"12-year selling in this alley\" (self-attest). Good craft honest.\nFrom \"别家叫老字号\" a line: Could use contrast with祖传, but internal slogan maybe weird.\n\nBest B candidate (recommended overall since target: trust craft):\nB1 IDENTITY? — hmm set IDENTITY as viewer belonging:\n「没吃过他家红烧肉，不算这条巷子的老主顾」 — feels like being老饕… \"这条巷子\" is their store, framing local neighborhood loyalty. Yet if not actually known by locals? weak.\nJust stick to direct craft options.\n\nB候选 titles:\n- B1 SITUATION/NARRATIVE (handmade factual): 「这锅肉，我们卖了12年」 \n- B2 CONTRADICTION (only modest): 「店才12年，但这锅肉我们一天没断过」 Actually \"店才12年\" self-effacing and addresses \"不要装老字号\" - not exactly contradiction but has slightly contrarian note. This line strongly fits user (do not say ancient secret but proud of modest age): shows longevity. video doesn't \"confirm\" unless caption included but candidate accepted. Provide condition: in the clip show the pot being lifted, in caption \"第12年\" or opening frames of store timeline? Hmm.\n- B3 IDENTITY:\n「你在这条巷子闻到过的红烧肉香，多半是这家」 — \"多半\" absurd.\nChose: B1 + another double:\n「第12年的那锅红烧肉，今天也照常出锅」 — simple and emotionally steady. Title recommendation? Might not \"gap\"; but gap? not enough wanting? \n- B2 \"每次走到这条巷子，都想拐进去吃的那锅肉\" - wish...\n\nWe need a headline that would actually perform with appetizing context: food titles on Douyin hook strongest with phrase \"这一勺下去\" or \"看着肉抖起来\". Could also combine: A为主 with craft claims as copy below.\n\nStrongest Douyin food title (sensory): 「这锅红烧肉一抖，我就知道今天这桌稳了」? \"稳了\" perhaps.\nOr tie in the \"出锅\" voice &amp; steamed: 「隔着屏幕，都怕这锅肉跑了」 humorous but no actual basis? express visual desire.\n\nOK, perhaps recommend title final:\n**「一碗卖到第12年的红烧肉，出锅前最后40秒」**? Wait combining too long across routes (claims + counting). If videoの caption says \"第12年\" and frame shows after-until-pan last 40 sec, title = summary again? No, it sets a scene of suspense. Doesn't overclaim. But holds cut-and-go? A \"第 12 年\".\n\nHmm, **题 candidate \"第12年，这锅肉还是这个做法\"** - good conveys.\n\nTitle restrictions: single title length≤15字 (Douyin recommendation). Our title options need carefully manage ≤15 Chinese characters:\n- 「这锅肉，我们卖了12年」= 10 (approx 10 chars? 这锅肉(3)，我们卖了(4)12年(3)=10+... fine).\n- 「红烧肉出锅的最后40秒」(11)\n- 「店才12年，肉一天没断过」? Count = 13 incl digits? ok.\n- 「一块五花肉，要这样收汁才够本帮」? Too tech? info.\n- **「卖了12年的一锅肉，出锅了」** uses 13.\n\nCover/首帧 design principles and selected moment (assumed): the frame of sauce being poured down from ladle, meat heaped, dark-red caramel glow; caption title small at top 150-safe; avoid text bottom300; the cover is for profile page: 大字 “红烧肉·12年” + 小字 “老城区巷子·8张桌”，背景那一锅肉的特写。Wait 首帧 cannot be same as cover per PP2? For Douyin (刷到型) cover low role; title/首帧 complementary: cover could simply identify store &amp; dish for profile (directory), no repetition conflict because it serves grid indexing, but avoid identical wording as title? The platform work: If no time making separate cover, Douyin auto first frame can be set to another strong frame.\nOn content: master title, subtitle rule, copy etc.\n\nSound placement: from PD planned whatever, no data → assume kitchen natural sounds (frying/boiling clatter), voiceover? We never know if voiceover exists. Sound指导: close-ups juice pour to be paired with quiet or amplified bubbling/steam, but need actual recording — probably not possible? Wait \"声音接住导演包，标最终进出点\" - no director pack → mark unavailable &amp; draft note: no director audio file provided; proposed if raw kitchen sound available: keep汁滚 and 碗碰灶 natural; avoid music overpowering sizzle; if no sound then备选 instrumental warm (电钢琴/手风琴?) hmm \"warm/old-town vibe\", but music choice risk layer C? Actually which music is \"in fashion\" would be layer C? choosing genre is production judgment, our skill might propose style not title of specific track. We can propose \"不压过现场声、节奏与切锅时间对齐的偏温暖/市井器乐\" but user's footage no music details &amp; platform trend not spec; avoid claiming. Give conditional craft.\n\ncomment/CTA content as above (LOW_RISK only): \n置顶: 「这锅肉我们家卖了12年，天天这么做。想知道做法/想问店里的，评论区问，我回复。 」Wait到店 question... fine but \"回复\" obligation.\nMaybe ask specific: \"你们家的红烧肉，是甜口还是咸口？我们这条巷子的答案是：都有一点。\" That would be knowledge. Hmm best concept: Ask a question to provoke recall: \"你记忆中最好吃的一顿红烧肉，是在哪吃的？\" This suits no-claim comments (memory sharing) &amp; creates comments. Reply for the cook opinion: \"我们家这锅肥的部分要抿着吃，你吃红烧肉先吃肥还是先