laim is legally the merchant. Skill requires facts based on provenance not necessarily third party. Reasonable basis exists: self-disclosure, is-verifiable 12yrs business mostly. Fact_refs absent but there. Actually facts are user statements, \"出自店主\" as origin is acceptable provenance for packaging and claims; the content owner confirms, so we can treat claims as valid (fact source = 店主本人有权证言+可出示辅证) -&gt; not fabricated. Good, fact_check_status PASS? We can't guarantee the claims true (Meituan ranking) but they're verifiable from merchant dashboard; but it's a claim of fact—owner states. Since sources are reliable... Fact-check maybe PASS as internally verified? Wait \"核验失败阻止交付... 核验只回答这句话有没有依据\"—We have basis/claims but not evidence; the double check should see the Meituan dashboard to PASS? Owner says \"这两年美团…销量第一\" — Should a packaging skill require screenshot? We don't have it. For safety: those facts won't be in titles? Actually we do not need Meituan claim in title/cover/copy at all; maybe exclude from above-the-line packaging except optional comment reply? Since it is a verifiable strong selling claim, but including in packaging would be extra external claim only owner's word. Since target just mentions. Might include it in publish copy? Perhaps no — \"这两年在美团\" sells to online diners; if store is a small street restaurant,美团 audience offline order; nice extra proof but not needed; if mentions, should present carefully. Also using \"美团同品类街销量第一\" in Douyin title may be seen as platform competitor mention, no? overcomplicating. Exclude from packaging or only comment optional if asked. If someone asks \"和别家比怎么样\" etc we probably not volunteer.\n\nSimilarly “本地菜场质量合格证” good for reassurance but not in title; put as optional comment reply in response to 食品安全: \"肉是每天本地菜场现买的，合格证贴在店里\" — factual owner statement.\n\nSo used_fact claims:\n-“卖12年”→ source owner. \n-“用自家腌黄酒糟卤打底”→source owner.\n-“8张桌/巷子里”→source owner (visual maybe from视频 if shows;)\n-“40秒出锅视频” itself for 